<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Topic//EN" "topic.dtd">
<topic id="auth-service-guide" xml:lang="en-us">
  <title id="topic-title">Authentication Service Configuration</title>
  <shortdesc id="shortdesc" outputclass="lead">This topic describes how to configure the Authentication Service, the
    available feature flags, and the REST endpoints that the service exposes.</shortdesc>
  <body>
    <section id="sec-overview">
      <title id="title-overview">Overview</title>
      <p id="p-intro">The Authentication Service authenticates the user credentials and returns a
        signed access token. It runs as a stateless component and can be scaled horizontally behind a load
        balancer.</p>
      <p id="p-arch" outputclass="architecture">Tokens are signed with the key configured in
        <codeph>auth.signing.key</codeph>. The service keeps no session data on the local disk and no
        session data in memory, so any instance can serve any request.</p>
      <p id="p-arch-note">The signing key is loaded once, at startup, and cached for the whole life
        of the process.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="sec-config">
      <title id="title-config">Configuring the service</title>
      <?oxy_comment_start author="Ana Popescu" timestamp="20260903T110500+0300" comment="Comment added by user A on a paragraph that user B rewrites." id="cmt-a-config-lead"?><p
        id="p-config-lead">The configuration file is read once, at startup. Restart the service
        after every change.</p><?oxy_comment_end?>
      <ul id="ul-prereq">
        <li id="li-prereq-1">A JDK 21 runtime, or later, is installed on the host.</li>
        <li id="li-prereq-2">The database schema is migrated to revision 47.</li>
        <li id="li-prereq-3">Port 8443 is open for inbound TLS traffic.</li>
        <li id="li-prereq-4">A signing key of at least 256 bits is available.</li>
      </ul>
      <ol id="ol-steps">
        <li id="li-step-1">Stop the running service
          instance<?oxy_insert_start author="Ana Popescu" timestamp="20260903T110600+0300"?> and wait
          for the open connections to drain<?oxy_insert_end?>.</li>
        <li id="li-step-2"><?oxy_comment_start author="Ana Popescu" timestamp="20260903T110700+0300" comment="Add the full path of the file for Windows installations." id="cmt-a-li-step-2"?><?oxy_comment_start author="Dan Ionescu" timestamp="20260903T110800+0300" comment="Reply from the second reviewer: the Windows path is documented in the installation topic." parentID="cmt-a-li-step-2" mid="1"?>Edit
            <filepath>conf/auth-service.properties</filepath> and set the signing
          key.<?oxy_comment_end mid="1"?><?oxy_comment_end?></li>
        <li id="li-step-3">Validate the configuration with <codeph>authctl verify</codeph>.</li>
        <li id="li-step-4">Start the service and check the health endpoint.</li>
        <li id="li-step-5">Confirm that the audit collector receives the first records.</li>
      </ol>
      <codeblock id="cb-config" outputclass="language-properties">auth.signing.key=file:/etc/auth/signing.pem
auth.token.ttl=7200
auth.audit.enabled=true</codeblock>
      <note id="note-warn" type="warning">Never commit the signing key to source control.</note>
    </section>
    <section id="sec-features">
      <title id="title-features">Feature flags</title>
      <?oxy_comment_start author="Ana Popescu" timestamp="20260903T110900+0300" comment="Checked against the release notes of 4.2." id="cmt-a-features-lead" flag="done"?><p
        id="p-features-lead">The following flags control the modules that are loaded at
        startup.</p><?oxy_comment_end?>
      <table id="table-features" frame="topbot" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
        <title id="title-table-features">Supported feature flags</title>
        <tgroup cols="4">
          <colspec colname="c1" colnum="1" colwidth="1.2*"/>
          <colspec colname="c2" colnum="2" colwidth="3*"/>
          <colspec colname="c3" colnum="3" colwidth="1*"/>
          <colspec colname="c4" colnum="4" colwidth="1.2*"/>
          <thead>
            <row id="row-features-head">
              <entry id="e-h-feature">Feature</entry>
              <entry id="e-h-desc">Description</entry>
              <entry id="e-h-status">Status</entry>
              <entry id="e-h-owner">Owner</entry>
            </row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row id="row-auth">
              <entry id="e-auth-name">Authentication</entry>
              <?oxy_comment_start author="Ana Popescu" timestamp="20260903T111000+0300" comment="Comment added by user A on a table cell: mention the SSO login as well." id="cmt-a-cell-auth-desc"?><entry
                id="e-auth-desc">Validates the user credentials against the configured user store
                and issues a signed access token that is valid for one hour. Both password and
                certificate based logins are supported.</entry><?oxy_comment_end?>
              <entry id="e-auth-status">Active</entry>
              <entry id="e-auth-owner">Identity team</entry>
            </row>
            <row id="row-authz">
              <entry id="e-authz-name">Authorization</entry>
              <entry id="e-authz-desc">Evaluates the role assignments of the authenticated user and
                returns the effective permission set for the requested resource.</entry>
              <entry id="e-authz-status">Deprecated</entry>
              <entry id="e-authz-owner">Platform team</entry>
            </row>
            <row id="row-log">
              <entry id="e-log-name">Logging</entry>
              <entry id="e-log-desc">Writes one structured audit record for every authentication
                attempt, including the client address, the user agent and the outcome of the
                attempt. Records are rotated daily.</entry>
              <entry id="e-log-status">Active</entry>
              <entry id="e-log-owner">Observability team</entry>
            </row>
            <row id="row-sec">
              <entry id="e-sec-name">Security</entry>
              <entry id="e-sec-desc">Applies the hardening profile: strict transport
                security,<?oxy_delete author="Ana Popescu" timestamp="20260903T111100+0300" content=" request rate limiting,"?>
                and rejection of weak cipher suites.</entry>
              <entry id="e-sec-status">Testing</entry>
              <entry id="e-sec-owner">Security team</entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </section>
    <section id="sec-endpoints">
      <title id="title-endpoints">REST endpoints</title>
      <p id="p-endpoints-lead">All endpoints are relative to the service context path and require a
        JSON request body.</p>
      <table id="table-endpoints" frame="topbot" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
        <?oxy_attributes frame="&lt;change type=&quot;modified&quot; oldValue=&quot;all&quot; author=&quot;Ana Popescu&quot; timestamp=&quot;20260903T111400+0300&quot; /&gt;"?>
        <title id="title-table-endpoints">Endpoints of the authentication API</title>
        <tgroup cols="3">
          <colspec colname="m1" colnum="1" colwidth="1*"/>
          <colspec colname="m2" colnum="2" colwidth="1.6*"/>
          <colspec colname="m3" colnum="3" colwidth="3*"/>
          <thead>
            <row id="row-ep-head">
              <entry id="e-h-method">Method</entry>
              <entry id="e-h-path">Path</entry>
              <entry id="e-h-epdesc">Description</entry>
            </row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row id="row-ep-login">
              <entry id="e-login-method"><codeph>POST</codeph></entry>
              <entry id="e-login-path"><filepath>/auth/login</filepath></entry>
              <entry id="e-login-desc">Exchanges the credentials sent in the
                <parmname>username</parmname> and <parmname>password</parmname> fields for an access
                token. Returns <codeph>401</codeph> when the credentials are rejected.</entry>
            </row>
            <row id="row-ep-refresh">
              <entry id="e-refresh-method"><codeph>POST</codeph></entry>
              <entry id="e-refresh-path"><filepath>/auth/refresh</filepath></entry>
              <entry id="e-refresh-desc">Issues a new access token for a still valid
                <parmname>refreshToken</parmname>. The old token is invalidated as described in
                <xref href="#auth-service-guide/sec-limits" format="dita">Limits</xref>.</entry>
            </row>
            <row id="row-ep-logout">
              <entry id="e-logout-method"><codeph>POST</codeph></entry>
              <entry id="e-logout-path"><filepath>/auth/logout</filepath></entry>
              <entry id="e-logout-desc">Invalidates the current access token. The client should also
                clear the token from its local storage.</entry>
            </row>
            <row id="row-ep-keys">
              <entry id="e-keys-method"><codeph>GET</codeph></entry>
              <entry id="e-keys-path"><filepath>/auth/keys</filepath></entry>
              <entry id="e-keys-desc">Returns the public part of the signing key so that downstream
                services can verify the tokens without calling the service.</entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </section>
    <section id="sec-limits">
      <title id="title-limits">Limits</title>
      <table id="table-limits" frame="topbot" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
        <title id="title-table-limits">Runtime limits</title>
        <tgroup cols="4">
          <colspec colname="l1" colnum="1" colwidth="1.4*"/>
          <colspec colname="l2" colnum="2" colwidth="1*"/>
          <colspec colname="l3" colnum="3" colwidth="1*"/>
          <colspec colname="l4" colnum="4" colwidth="2.6*"/>
          <thead>
            <row id="row-lim-head">
              <entry id="e-h-param">Parameter</entry>
              <entry id="e-h-default">Default</entry>
              <entry id="e-h-max">Maximum</entry>
              <entry id="e-h-notes">Notes</entry>
            </row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row id="row-lim-ttl">
              <entry id="e-lim-ttl-name">Token lifetime</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-ttl-def">7200</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-ttl-max">86400</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-ttl-notes">Expressed in seconds. Longer lifetimes increase the window
                in which a leaked token can be replayed.</entry>
            </row>
            <row id="row-lim-rate">
              <entry id="e-lim-rate-name">Requests per minute</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-rate-def">600</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-rate-max">6000</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-rate-notes">Counted per client address. Requests over the limit are
                answered with <codeph>429</codeph>.</entry>
            </row>
            <row id="row-lim-burst">
              <entry id="e-lim-burst-name">Burst size</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-burst-def">50</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-burst-max">500</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-burst-notes">Number of requests that are accepted above the steady
                rate before throttling starts.</entry>
            </row>
            <row id="row-lim-pool">
              <entry id="e-lim-pool-name">Connection pool size</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-pool-def">20</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-pool-max">400</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-pool-notes">Applies to the connection pool of the user store.</entry>
            </row>
            <?oxy_insert_start author="Ana Popescu" timestamp="20260903T111200+0300"?>
            <row id="row-lim-clock">
              <entry id="e-lim-clock-name">Clock skew</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-clock-def">30</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-clock-max">300</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-clock-notes">Tolerated difference, in seconds, between the clock of
                the token issuer and the clock of the verifier.</entry>
            </row>
            <?oxy_insert_end?>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </section>
    <section id="sec-deploy">
      <title id="title-deploy">Deployment profiles</title>
      <p id="p-deploy-lead">Three deployment profiles are supported out of the
        box<?oxy_insert_start author="Ana Popescu" timestamp="20260903T111300+0300"?>, and a custom
        profile can be derived from any of them<?oxy_insert_end?>.</p>
      <ul id="ul-profiles">
        <li id="li-profile-prod">Production
          <ul id="ul-prod-details">
            <li id="li-prod-1">At least three instances, in separate availability zones.</li>
            <li id="li-prod-2">Audit records are shipped to the central collector.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li id="li-profile-dev">Development
          <ul id="ul-dev-details">
            <li id="li-dev-1">A single instance with an in-memory user store.</li>
            <li id="li-dev-2">Audit logging is disabled.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li id="li-profile-stage">Staging
          <ul id="ul-stage-details">
            <li id="li-stage-1">Two instances behind a load balancer.</li>
            <li id="li-stage-2">A shared PostgreSQL user store.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section id="sec-trouble">
      <title id="title-trouble">Troubleshooting</title>
      <dl id="dl-trouble">
        <dlentry id="dlentry-401">
          <dt id="dt-401">All requests are answered with 401</dt>
          <dd id="dd-401">The signing key is not the same on all instances. Redeploy the shared key
            and restart the instances one by one.</dd>
        </dlentry>
        <dlentry id="dlentry-slow">
          <dt id="dt-slow">Token issuing is slow</dt>
          <dd id="dd-slow">The user store is the usual bottleneck. Check the size of the connection
            pool and the latency of the store.</dd>
        </dlentry>
      </dl>
      <p id="p-trouble-end">If the problem persists, collect the audit log and open a support ticket
        for the Identity team.</p>
    </section>
  </body>
</topic>
